  "body": "In particular for JavaScript string, see #73, we need something like code-unit length from HTML (and then remove that from HTML and use our new concept).\r\n\r\nEither we define size and for JavaScript string it's the number of code units and for scalar value string it's the number of scalar values, or size is always code points and we have code-unit size just for JavaScript strings. The latter is probably slightly better since it makes it more explicit?",
